--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WEB SOURCE SHAPE (read end-to-end — covenant #3)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
GrafanaPanelPage.tsx is a manual Grafana-panel JSON builder. It owns NO API data source (the
manifest record lists dataSources: [] — "renders from navigation values / local state"). Its render
tree:
  • usePageTitle(t('powerGrafana.title')) + a PageTitle + an intro <p> (t('powerGrafana.intro')).
  • <AINLGrafanaPanel onApply={handleApplyAiDraft} /> — the opt-in Helix natural-language drafter
    (a SEPARATE, already-shipped parity unit, P4 shared surface 0033, whose 14 Apple files live in
    apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/AINLGrafanaPanel.*). It is propose-only: handleApplyAiDraft
    copies JSON.stringify(draft.panel, null, 2) into the editor; the browser never pushes to Grafana.
  • GlassPanel 1 — "Manual panel JSON editor": a <Textarea> (rows=12, spellCheck off, aria-label
    powerGrafana.editor.label), a primary "Copy to clipboard" + secondary "Clear" (both disabled when
    canCopy=false), and an amber status <span role="status"> driven by statusMessage. handleCopy
    branches: empty -> copyEmpty; no navigator.clipboard -> copyUnavailable; writeText resolved ->
    copySuccess; writeText threw -> copyFailed. The JSON persists to localStorage 'ai.grafanaPanel.draft'.
  • GlassPanel 2 — "Curated panel types": name-sorted CURATED_PANEL_TYPES (8: timeseries/stat/gauge/
    table/barchart/heatmap/piechart/logs), each a bordered card name(mono cyan)+description, in a
    grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 grid.
  • GlassPanel 3 — "Curated datasource types": name-sorted CURATED_DATASOURCE_TYPES (2: postgres
    uid=tesla-postgres, prometheus uid=tesla-prometheus), each "name · uid=<uid>" (cyan name / muted
    sep / green uid) + description, single-column.
  • GlassPanel 4 — "Curated table catalog (postgres targets)": name-sorted CURATED_TABLES (5: drives,
    charging_sessions, vehicles, alerts, signal_log_view) each name(mono cyan)+description + a wrapping
    column list (name green · type — description). SI-canonical columns (distance_m / energy_used_wh /
    avg_speed_mps …), per Phase-48 SI canon.
The three catalogs are install-wide-static (the web source documents this) — duplicated, not fetched.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OUTPUT PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/PowerUser/GrafanaPanelPage.swift`.
That dir does NOT exist as a compiled *page* home in this repo. The repo's real, compiled page home —
where the DIRECT sibling power-user page SqlPlaygroundPage ships, and which project.yml lists as the
`Sources` source group — is `apps/apple/Sources/Features/PowerUser/**`. The page therefore ships there
(the faithful equivalent of the prompt's `Features/PowerUser`), decomposed exactly as the sibling
SqlPlayground decomposes (page / catalog-views / model / sample / route-registration). Strings ship in
the platform catalog `apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This is the
SAME reconciliation the accepted sibling notifications-Archived + power-user-SqlPlayground P7 logs
recorded. The hosted AINLGrafanaPanel surface is REUSED (DRY), not re-implemented.

ROUTE HOSTING: web `/power/grafana` is nested (two segments). A dedicated `.powerGrafana` AppRoute case
is added (pathSegment `power/grafana` -> `.path` `/power/grafana` matching web exactly; System group
alongside `.powerSql` + `.powerUser`; SF Symbol `chart.xyaxis.line`). `AppRouteParser` aliases
`/power/grafana` -> `.powerGrafana` (required — the generic first-segment fallback resolves `power`,
which no route owns; mirrors the sibling `/power/sql` alias). `GrafanaPanelRouteRegistration` hosts the
page, chained into `\.routeHosts` in TeslaSyncApp.swift right after `SqlPlaygroundRouteRegistration`.
The nav-label string `route.powerGrafana` ("Grafana Panel Builder") is added to the catalog (the
sidebar reads `route.<rawValue>`). So the page is reachable via the System-group sidebar entry and any
`/power/grafana` deep link. (Navigation registration + the string catalog are allowed files.)

DATA-STATE NOTE: the manifest declares exactly one data state — `success` — because the page binds NO
API source (the catalogs are compiled constants, the editor is local state). There is therefore no
page-level loading/empty/error region to render (the embedded AINLGrafanaPanel owns its OWN
gate/loading/streaming/error/stale states as its separate parity unit). The page's `success` state =
the editor + the three always-rendered catalog panels bound through the @Observable model; no region is
ever blank.

